}

\p{Open after wave 6 (M6), most valuable first:}

\ul{
\li{\strong{Declarations that enter eager reduction go to the reference engine} (F26): 6,711 units of mathlib (0.93 \%), 11-12 \% of the worker CPU there (P8), 11 declarations = 18 \% of the machine's ticks on the Cedar slice (M5). An official-exact way to keep them: pair entries tagged with the mode they were derived in and read only in that mode (then every answer is the official DIRECT answer of that mode, which the official cache can only extend), WHNF / CORE memo words of OPEN values neither read nor written under ER (M3's offer, 15:34Z), and a session of its own; to be attacked by S before it replaces the decline.}
\li{\strong{The intern tables of giant sessions} (M1, 15:58Z): on reachability 39 \% of the process waits for slots of 64-256 MiB tables. A young set in front of \code{\verb~|vtab~} / \code{\verb~|rtab~} (new entries in a small table, moved in batches) and 4x growth above 2^20 slots are \code{\verb~|Machine~} designs (reset and growth assume every record and run is in the table); not started.}
\li{\strong{Slabs outside the Java heap} (growth by \code{\verb~|mremap~} instead of copy + page faults; F25): needs one accessor for \code{\verb~|m.vh[..]~} / \code{\verb~|m.rs[..]~}; not started.}
\li{\strong{A later pass of \code{\verb~|-X passes~} gets a new \code{\verb~|MachineEngine~}} (T2, 16:20Z): the code store and a compiled tier start cold in every pass; a per-\code{\verb~|Store~} code store inside the machine, or the driver keeping the engine, is open.}
\li{\code{\verb~|Op.HOST_DEPTH~} 2048 (M3, 15:34Z: reachability with \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} writes 1.5 \% of its call events as frames at 128): not changed; needs the deep tests on a 512 KiB stack at that depth.}
\li{Next candidates for the default set, ready per their owners: \code{\verb~|pchk~}, \code{\verb~|match~}, \code{\verb~|joint~} (M5), \code{\verb~|lazyeval~} (M4), \code{\verb~|same~} (M4, after S), \code{\verb~|code,casetrees~} (M7: reachability 8.79 -> 1.56 s). \code{\verb~|SWITCHES.md~} says how a default changes.}
\li{\code{\verb~|MachineProvider.priority()~} is still 10. Before it is raised: the items the orchestrator listed at 16:14Z (done: the tick bound, F31) and S's open row S-F3 (levels, both engines).}
}

\p{Not done / not measured (M6):}

\ul{
\li{\code{\verb~|pubcheck~} is a set of id checks (\code{\verb~|Debug.pubTerm / pubLevel / pubList / pubConst~}) for M5 and M7 to call when they publish a record; no block or fact record exists yet, so nothing calls them.}
\li{Engine-wide tables under contention (staging step 6) are untouched.}
\li{\code{\verb~|hostDepth~} as a field against a compile-time constant, and the masked TICK line against the plain one (skeleton notes S3, S4), were not measured in isolation; only the bound's value was (F22).}
\li{\code{\verb~|memocheck~} hooks exist in \code{\verb~|Eval~} (M2), \code{\verb~|Reduce~} (M3), \code{\verb~|Conv~} (M4) and \code{\verb~|Infer~} (M5, since 10:17Z). The published INST hook of \code{\verb~|Eval~} re-computes at HOLE, which is wrong for the COD memo \code{\verb~|Infer.k_lam4~} writes on a PII whose body reads its variable (requested from M2 09:17Z and 10:05Z); until it is fixed M5 does not write that memo while the mode is on, so the mode does not audit it. The memocheck run of Init in the README is with the published tree of 10:34Z; earlier runs used a one-line local fix of that hook.}
\li{No test runs a fatal fault inside a TRY of a real judgment: v0 has no speculative segment (\code{\verb~|SW_PROBES~} off). The rule is tested on the toy judgments (\code{\verb~|ControlTest~}, \code{\verb~|M6FacadeTest~}, \code{\verb~|M6DebugTest~}).}
\li{One \code{\verb~|Machine~} allocates about 20 MiB when its session is created (RSS of a one-unit run: 98 MB against 77 MB with the reference engine); the strict engine's sessions are allocated as eagerly as the warm ones.}
}
}
